1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,376
Every morning at six, I type the final words for people who do not know they are dying.

2
00:00:05,676 --> 00:00:12,900
My boss calls it editing history. I call it pulling the trigger with a backlit keyboard and a cup of cold coffee.

3
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:20,496
The rules are simple. Once I press publish on their life story, their heart stops beating within the hour.

4
00:00:20,796 --> 00:00:28,236
I thought I was playing God. I enjoyed the quiet power humming beneath my fingertips every single lonely night.

5
00:00:28,536 --> 00:00:35,040
Then tonight, a new file appeared in my queue with no name, no photo, and a blinking cursor.

6
00:00:35,340 --> 00:00:42,108
I scrolled down to check the author details. My own home address stared back from the system metadata.

7
00:00:42,408 --> 00:00:49,704
My biography was already written down to the exact second. It described the exact clothes I am wearing.

8
00:00:50,004 --> 00:00:57,492
The final sentence read: He sat in the dark, staring at the screen, waiting for the inevitable blackout.

9
00:00:57,792 --> 00:01:04,968
My fingers moved on their own, hovering over the keyboard to write the last word of my life.

10
00:01:05,268 --> 00:01:09,948
If I am the author of the final paragraph, who wrote the period at the end of mine?
